####Information for a sample site simulation######

This file contains information to run a sample site, 
US-FCl (Fort Collins, CO, USA)

1) Untar the sample driver data
   (tar -xzvf sample.tgz)
   This creates the directory sib4_sample

2) Compile SiB4
   In sib4_corral/code directory, type 'make'
   Changes may need to be made to the Makefile
   if it does not compile

3) Move the executable to the main sib4_corral directory
   (in sib4_corral/code, 'mv SiB4D ..')

4) Change back into the main directory, 
   (just in sib4_corral), then run by typing:
   ./SiB4D info/sites/sib4_sample/namel_sibdrv


The namelist file (sib4_sample/namel_sibdrv)
if currently setup to run 2016 and save
hourly, daily, and monthly output.

The variables being saved are specified in the
sib4_corral/input/sib_outopts file.
The default is a relatively minimal selection.

The output will be saved in the 
sib4_corral/info/sib4_sample/output directory,
so for this to run you will need to have
write permissions to that directory.

This sample uses the restart file sib_requib.nc.
To create your own restart file, in the namel_sibdrv
you need to set 'spinup = .true.'
I'd also recommend spinning up over a longer
period of time, rather than a single year.
So change the startyear to 1997 
(uses all the provided data).

With the spinup_default flag set to true,
this will start from default (minimum leaf pool only),
and iterate until equilibrium pools calculated change 
less than the spinup_threshold value in an iteration.

The output will go to the directory listed in the out_path.
To then use the new spinup values, just move the sib_equibsxx.nc
file (numbered sequentially, so you'll want the last one)
to your driver directory.


